  "details": "i feel like it would be useful and easy to implement a primitive chatting system that would essentially work like a join request without a join request. you would be able to customize the \"request\" message without sending an invite. ive found myself just sending join requests to ask someone a question in game (usually before actually joining them) and i feel like it could be implemented nicely. for example: when requesting someone to join you could have a small box to tick to actually ask for an invite or not along with whatever message you have typed or just an additional box called \"message\" or \"ping\" on profiles. VRC+ users could still get the ability to send pictures or a bigger character limit. same could go for groups, like a big group chat that you could send invite requests through.",
